@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · Routing table：`high` is the default ceiling. V4.1-Flash drives effort from an internal 1–100 scalar and exposes
three preset names; `high` corresponds to roughly 75, which is where the published effort curve is
still steep. Pushing past it costs about 1.6–1.8x the output tokens for a marginal gain.

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · Authorization scopes, the model pool and task presets (v0.5)：```yaml
pool:
  - { id: deepseek-official/deepseek-flash, cost: 1, tier: cheap }
  - { id: deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-pro, cost: 8, tier: strong, maxPerTask: 3 }
  - { id: deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp, cost: 1, tags: [vision] }

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · Multiple brands: grouping, automatic pricing and the cross-brand guard (v0.14.0)：Routes: `POST /model-router/cross { sessionId, action }` (`allow` / `once` / `never`),
`POST /model-router/pool/auto-price { fetch }` and `POST /model-router/prices`; `/state` gains `cross` and
`prices`.

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · The observation baseline: telemetry, /stats, /router replay and ETag (v0.15.0)：**Host self-check.** At boot the plugin verifies its host contracts: `sessionProjections` is required, while a missing
`webServer`/`commands`/`llm` only degrades features. Missing pieces are logged once and surfaced in
`GET /state.compat.missing`, so the panel can say the host is incomplete.

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · Prices, hard dates and catalog drift (v0.15.1)：**Priced decisions.** `router.decision/1` carries `usage.split`, `usage.costUsd` and a `usage.price` snapshot
(currency, unit, `effectiveFrom`, `peak`, source and the four rates in force), taken at the step's own timestamp - a
replayed step is priced at the rate that was actually charged, not at today's.

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · Prices, hard dates and catalog drift (v0.15.1)：**Cost ledger in `/stats`.** `totals` and every `by*` row carry `tokens`, `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`,
`cacheReadTokens`, `cacheWriteTokens`, `reasoningTokens`, `costUsd`, `pricedSteps` and `unpricedSteps`. An event
written before 0.15.1 has no split and is counted as unpriced, never as free.

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · Channel health, spend limits and the peak window (v0.16.1)：```yaml
channels:  { failover: false, failThreshold: 3, cooldownMs: 60000, quarantineMs: 86400000, fingerprint: true }
budget:    { mode: off, sessionTokens: 0, sessionUsd: 0, dayUsd: 0, monthUsd: 0, softRatio: 0.8 }
peakPolicy: inform    # off | inform | shift
crossCost: { maxMultiple: 3, scoreMargin: 5 }

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · A feedback loop, a classifier that admits doubt, and exploration (v0.17.1)：`/stats.feedback` aggregates the file rather than the session — totals and per-label counts, `overrides` (every label that
is not `just-right`) with their share, `outcomes` (how many were answered, and how many of those changed the route), and
`byClass`, so a class that keeps earning "too weak" is visible next to the class that keeps earning "too expensive".

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · What 1.0.0 actually promises (v1.0.0)：Deliberately not in this version: splitting the browser bundle into a build artifact, and a CI matrix
against two host versions. Both are infrastructure work that does not change what the router decides,
and both are recorded as deferred in `PLAN.md` rather than implied by the version number.

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · The mode pool and a pinned relay effort (v1.1.0)：Two additions that answer two very different problems: DSH ships four agent presets and the router had
nothing to say about them, and relay gateways pin a model to one reasoning word and used to receive
whatever the ladder produced.

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · The five rules：Task boundaries come from `agent/inbox/claimed`, which is what actually opens a new piece of work.
When a task ends on an unresolved failure, the next one inherits a single hesitant step up — and only
if it is engineering or hard work. A one-line "translate this" never inherits a crash.

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · Tool loops no longer pin the effort at high (v0.9.0)：Measured before: `帮我把这个文件里的日志改成中文` ran `standard`/`low` at 0 tools, then
`engineering`/`high` at 1, 3, 6, 12 and 25 tools for the rest of the task; `翻译一下这句话` with one
tool also went to `high`.

@neptune810/dsh-model-router README · The model catalog：Routing thresholds are code; model facts are data. `catalog/model-catalog.yaml` is the source of truth
for what each addressable model costs, which reasoning-effort words it accepts, what its context window is,
which channels carry it and what is scheduled to change — 19 models with an evidence date, written so that
`unknown` stays `unknown` instead of being guessed. It is validated against
`schema/model-catalog.schema.json` and compiled into `lib/catalog.js` by `scripts/build-catalog.py`.
The generated module is committed and never edited by hand.
